  "body": "Found by the release QA swarm (#2582) on **v0.24.0** with SolidCraft 0.45.0, driven through MCP by a Codex agent (len). Part: 80 x 60 x 18 base (R5 vertical edges) + half-ellipsoid boss (unit sphere scaled 25/18/12) with an R2 root fillet and an R3 runner; one closed 14-face body, 97165.69 mm³.\n\n## What happens\n`import_model` of the SolidCraft STEP reports 54953 facets with no reduced-fidelity or open-mesh notice. Every 3D operation then refuses at generate:\n\n```\nWaterline6: the source model cannot be sliced: the mesh is open at z = 19.687500000000004: 2 dangling chord ends\n```\nSame for a 3D Pocket (adaptive), Scallop and Pencil. SolidCraft reopens the STEP as one closed body (volume within 0.0001 mm³). An STL export of the same body imports and slices, so the STEP path is the problem (tessellation or slicing).\n\nThe same message hits a modelled helical thread (#3023), so this may be one root cause; #917 (STEP through solidcore, merged after the tag) may change it.\n\n## Expected\nA closed STEP body imports as a closed mesh, or the import itself warns that the mesh has open edges (instead of every operation failing later).\n\n## Reproduce (on len)\n`/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q02-3d-mold/q02-step-import-failure.camproj` -> `open_project`, `generate {name:\"Waterline6\"}`. STEP: `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q02-3d-mold/q02-3d-mold.step`; SolidCraft build script `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q02-3d-mold/q02-build.json`; report `/home/mikekinney/qa/runs/20261120-q02-3d-mold/REPORT.md` (problem 2).\n\nNot checked on current main.\n\nDone means: this STEP imports and a 3D op on it generates (or the import names the open edges), pinned by a test on the recorded STEP.\n",
